{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And there we saw the Nephilim.</b> One may say: Nephilim means tall, like 'mountain of lofty height' (הר נופל) in יבול of Job, which they interpreted as tall — the sense of Nephilim." "<b>Bnei Anak.</b> Rashi explained: they necklace (מעניקין) the sun with their height, because of their exceedingly tall stature — they are as though their neck pierces and chokes the opening through which the sun emerges. Thus Rashi explained in chapter 'Eilu Nemarim.'" "<b>Like grasshoppers.</b> Not literally like grasshoppers, but very small. And so is the way of Scripture to speak: 'and its inhabitants are like grasshoppers' (וגו')."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The reference is to Job 40:17 (הרים יבול נופל); rendered the phrase hyper-literally as Chizkuni cites it.", 1 "Chizkuni explicitly names Rashi here; the wordplay on ענק (necklace/strangle) is preserved as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:53.309811231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}